# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Gun Spa — environment variables
# Copy to .env.local for local dev. On Replit, add these under Tools → Secrets.
# Everything is optional: with no variables set the site runs fully with an
# embedded Postgres (PGlite) in ./.data and confirms reservations without
# payment ("pay on arrival").
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Public origin override (Stripe redirect URLs, emails, sitemap, Open Graph tags).
# Production builds default to https://gunspa.com (canonicalUrl in src/lib/config/site.ts) and
# development uses the Replit workspace domain or localhost, so this is only needed for a staging
# address. Replit's deployment builder does not pass secrets to `next build`, so the prerendered
# sitemap and share tags cannot read it there anyway.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://staging.gunspa.com

# Postgres connection string. On Replit: create a PostgreSQL database from the
# Database tool and this is set for you. Leave unset to use the embedded dev DB.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:pass@host:5432/dbname

# Front desk (/admin) password, 6+ characters. Required to view/manage reservations and members.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me

# Signs member and admin session cookies. A long random string (openssl rand -base64 32).
# Required in production: member sign-in refuses to run without it. Never derived from ADMIN_PASSWORD.
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# --- Stripe (optional; enables card payment at reservation time) -------------
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...   (from the webhook endpoint you create for /api/stripe/webhook)

# --- Email confirmations via Resend (optional) --------------------------------
# RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
# EMAIL_FROM="The Gun Spa <reservations@gunspa.com>"
# EMAIL_BCC=frontdesk@gunspa.com
